%% Two parameters are two distinct abstract types: "The abstract instance of a
%% parameterised procedure declaration replaces each type parameter by a
%% distinct abstract type" (TGLP parameterized-types.tex, Definition
%% "Parametrically Well-Typed"), and an abstract type "matches only itself"
%% (Definition "Abstract Type").  cast/2 hands A?, at X, through id/2 to B, at
%% Y: no instantiation of id/2 makes both pairs well-typed with subtyping, so
%% cast/2 is not parametrically well-typed, and go/1's call, which supplies
%% String for Y and no type for X, is refused.  Until 2026-10-12 the two
%% abstract types, each with an empty automaton, were one type by automata
%% alone: cast/2 was certified, X left open, and go(S) gave S = 5, an Integer
%% where go/1 hands out a String.
procedure(T) id(T?, T).
id(X, X?).
procedure(X, Y) cast(X?, Y).
cast(A, B?) :- id(A?, B).
procedure go(String).
go(S?) :- cast(5, S).
